walking by himself without any help  Prince Philip seemed happy and relaxed  leaving the king Edward the seventh  Hospital the ninety eight year old was  picked up at a back entrance to give him  more privacy but the press were still  able to get the pictures that we wanted  four days after going in for treatment  to a pre-existing medical condition he  was finally on his way back to Norfolk  for Christmas with his family it came as  the palace released extracts of the  Queen's Christmas message after a  turbulent year both politically with  brexit and personally with family dramas  the theme is reconciliation she will say  how small steps taken in faith and in  Hope can overcome long-held differences  and deep-seated divisions to bring  harmony and understanding the path of  course is not always smooth and may at  times this year have felt quite bumpy  but small steps can make a world of  difference she talks about this year's  d-day commemorations and how in the true  spirit of reconciliation those who'd  formerly been enemies came together  adding that by being willing to put  differences behind us and move forward  together we honor the freedom and  democracy once one for us is so great a  cost her message also appears to be not  her own difficult year from Prince  Philip's car accident to Prince Andrew  giving up his royal duties because the  Jeffrey Epstein scandal and Prince Harry  and Megan being criticized for using  private jets and taking legal action  against the press the interview that  that the Duke of York gave was a  disaster and I'm you know I think nobody  understands why he did it he seemed  undecided he contradicted himself and he  made himself you know a laughingstock  which is really sad this new footage of  the Queen and her three heirs will also  appear in the Christmas message with the  monarch Prince Charles Prince William  and Prince George making Christmas  puddings for the British Legion for  generations working together even if  six-year-old George does look a little  uncertain about the small talk it shows  that away from the concerns  about Prince Phillip the Royals have  been preparing for Christmas as usual  the Duke and Duchess of Sussex and their  son Archie sending out this electronic  cart they won't be at Sandringham for  Christmas but a helicopter leaving  Buckingham Palace was confirmation that  Prince Phillip was heading for Norfolk  shortly after he arrived the palace  issued a statement saying he wanted to  thank everyone for their good wishes  Rhiannon Mills Sky News
 

